Uwe <mail@wespec.de> wrote:
>As far as I now its more historical. Nethack is a D&D derived game,
>where the maximal strength is 18. Having strength of 18 gives you a
>special percentage of doing superstrength-actions (like in a circus).

This is not quite right. The percentile value (for classes that get it) is
rolled if a strength of 18 is generated, and effectively represents a
smaller number of strength values between 18 and 19 (for instance, 18/01
is _exactly_ the same as 18/50 and all values in between); the percentile
value is never used directly.

The whole system is utterly perverse and has thankfully been thrown away
in the 3rd edition of the game. It makes a little more sense in NetHack
where it makes it more difficult to gain strength once you already have a
value over 18, but even there the break points - 18/01, 18/51, 18/76 and
then more closely spaced mean that it is most difficult to gain strength
just after passing 18, but then becomes easier again.
